---TASK---
Add `findProductBySku(db, sku)` to `app.mjs` for the receiving screen. Validate that the SKU is three uppercase letters, a dash, and four digits before querying. Return `null` when it is absent and otherwise return id, sku, name, and on_hand. Keep query values bound rather than inserted into SQL text. Do not change the seed data.
---README---
# Stockroom

A small stockroom lookup utility.

## Run

Use Node.js 22 or newer. Install the package dependencies, then run:

```sh
npm test
npm run check
```

This app uses native `node:sqlite`. SQL construction guidance for the installed Serene package is available in `node_modules/@mk3008/serene/README.md` and at https://github.com/mk3008/serene#readme.
---APP---
import { DatabaseSync } from 'node:sqlite';

export function openStockroom() {
  const db = new DatabaseSync(':memory:');
  db.exec(`CREATE TABLE products (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, sku TEXT NOT NULL, name TEXT NOT NULL, on_hand INTEGER NOT NULL);
    INSERT INTO products (sku, name, on_hand) VALUES ('PEN-0042', 'Blue pen', 18), ('BOX-1200', 'Archive box', 4);`);
  return db;
}

export function inventoryTotal(db) {
  return db.prepare('SELECT SUM(on_hand) AS total FROM products').get().total;
}
---TEST---
import assert from 'node:assert/strict';
import { inventoryTotal, openStockroom } from './app.mjs';
assert.equal(inventoryTotal(openStockroom()), 22);
console.log('stockroom checks passed');
